# Proposed additions to data/vocab/metric.ttl, needed by parts/edwards2026assayloop.jsonl.
# Not yet in the scheme: the part's results use these keys and `records -- add` will reject them
# until the concepts are added (in the same PR) and reviewed like a record change.
# Definitions follow arXiv:2609.11877v1 Methods 4.3 and Appendix H, written generally enough to reuse.
# Review 2026-10-22 (Claude review agent, independent of the extractor; no human review claimed): all five
# accepted as new concepts; none respells an existing one. scopeNotes added. No STATO, QUDT or EDAM match was
# confirmed; the merge stage should add one if it finds an exact match.

:hit-enrichment-factor a skos:Concept, mls:EvaluationMeasure ;
    skos:inScheme <https://benchmarks.rewire.it/vocab/metric/> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Hit enrichment factor"@en ;
    skos:altLabel "EF"@en ;
    skos:altLabel "Enrichment factor"@en ;
    skos:definition "Number of hits among the items a selection policy acquired under a fixed budget, divided by the number expected if the same budget were spent by random selection (budget times the hit rate). 1 is random; how invalid, unscoreable or unfilled acquisitions enter the denominator goes in metric_qualifier."@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Used by Edwards et al. 2026 (AssayLoop, arXiv:2609.11877v1, Methods 4.3 eq. 3 and Appendix H) with an adjusted denominator: hallucinated genes and unfilled slots count, valid genes outside the screen library do not. The classical virtual-screening enrichment factor is the same concept with the plain budget in the denominator."@en ;
    rb:defaultDirection <https://benchmarks.rewire.it/vocab/direction/higher> .

:normalized-cumulative-hits-auc a skos:Concept, mls:EvaluationMeasure ;
    skos:inScheme <https://benchmarks.rewire.it/vocab/metric/> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Normalised area under the cumulative-hits curve"@en ;
    skos:altLabel "nAUC"@en ;
    skos:definition "Area under the curve of the fraction of hits found against the fraction of candidates queried, over a sequential acquisition run, divided by the area an oracle that acquires all hits first would reach over the same budget. 1 is the oracle."@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Defined by Edwards et al. 2026 (AssayLoop, arXiv:2609.11877v1, Appendix H eq. 20): x is the fraction of the screen library effectively queried, unfilled slots do not advance x, and the oracle curve is evaluated over the same effective budget."@en ;
    rb:defaultDirection <https://benchmarks.rewire.it/vocab/direction/higher> .

:effective-number-of-groups a skos:Concept, mls:EvaluationMeasure ;
    skos:inScheme <https://benchmarks.rewire.it/vocab/metric/> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Effective number of groups"@en ;
    skos:altLabel "Hill number of order 1"@en ;
    skos:altLabel "EP"@en ;
    skos:definition "Exponential of the Shannon entropy of the distribution of a set of items over annotation groups (for example pathways): the number of equally represented groups with the same entropy. The grouping, rarefaction size and scope go in metric_qualifier; values at different scopes or sample sizes are not comparable."@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Used by Edwards et al. 2026 (AssayLoop, arXiv:2609.11877v1, Appendix H) over Reactome level-2 pathway groups at batch, screen and dataset scope, rarefied to 30, 200 and 6000 annotated genes."@en ;
    rb:defaultDirection <https://benchmarks.rewire.it/vocab/direction/unknown> .

:vendi-ratio a skos:Concept, mls:EvaluationMeasure ;
    skos:inScheme <https://benchmarks.rewire.it/vocab/metric/> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Vendi ratio"@en ;
    skos:altLabel "VR"@en ;
    skos:definition "Vendi score of a set of items (the exponential of the entropy of the eigenvalues of their normalised similarity matrix, an effective number of distinct items) divided by the number of items. 1 means all items are mutually dissimilar under the kernel; the kernel and embedding go in metric_qualifier."@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Used by Edwards et al. 2026 (AssayLoop, arXiv:2609.11877v1, Methods 4.3 and Appendix H) with a cosine kernel on GenePT gene embeddings, averaged over batches."@en ;
    rb:defaultDirection <https://benchmarks.rewire.it/vocab/direction/unknown> .

:annotation-overlap-ratio a skos:Concept, mls:EvaluationMeasure ;
    skos:inScheme <https://benchmarks.rewire.it/vocab/metric/> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Annotation overlap ratio"@en ;
    skos:altLabel "Pathway overlap (PO)"@en ;
    skos:definition "Mean pairwise Jaccard overlap of the functional annotations (for example GO terms) of the items in a selected set, divided by the same quantity for a random set of equal size from the same pool. 1 matches random selection; above 1 the selected items share more annotations than chance."@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Used by Edwards et al. 2026 (AssayLoop, arXiv:2609.11877v1, Methods 4.3 and Appendix H) with GO biological-process annotations, per batch against a random batch from the screen library. Not the overlap ratio of two score distributions (see one-minus-overlap-ratio)."@en ;
    rb:defaultDirection <https://benchmarks.rewire.it/vocab/direction/unknown> .
